## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical, beginner-friendly construction of a data pipeline with common tasks: deduplication, validation, timestamp handling, and partitioned Parquet, plus testing and monitoring.

## Key Concepts
- JSON Lines parsing
- Idempotent deduplication
- Data quality checks (required fields, types)
- Timestamp normalization to UTC
- Parquet writing and date partitioning
- Basic testing and observability

## Code Example
```javascript
const fs = require('fs');
const readline = require('readline');
(async () => {
  const rl = readline.createInterface({ input: fs.createReadStream('logs.jsonl'), crlfDelay: Infinity });
  const seen = new Set();
  for await (const line of rl) {
    const obj = JSON.parse(line);
    if (!obj.user_id || !obj.timestamp || !obj.path || !obj.status) continue;
    const key = `${obj.timestamp}|${obj.user_id}|${obj.path}`;
    if (seen.has(key)) continue;
    seen.add(key);
    // normalization and persistence would occur here
  }
})();
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale this for multi-region logs?
- What metrics and alerts would you add for production reliability?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design multi-tenant data contracts, runtime validation, privacy masking, and governance in a real-time setting. Also probes trade-offs between Spark and Flink, plus testing strategies and observability.

## Key Concepts

- Runtime data contracts per tenant
- Per-tenant masking/redaction strategies
- GDPR deletion and data sovereignty
- Schema evolution in lakehouse (Iceberg/Parquet)
- Policy engine governance (e.g., OPA)
- Spark Structured Streaming vs Flink trade-offs
- Testing, monitoring, data quality

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo runtime contract check
function validateRecord(record, contract) {
  for (const field of Object.keys(contract.fields)) {
    if (!record.hasOwnProperty(field) && contract.fields[field].required) {
      throw new Error(`Missing required field ${field}`);
    }
  }
  // redaction example
  if (contract.mask) {
    for (const f of contract.mask) {
      if (record[f]) record[f] = "REDACTED";
    }
  }
  return record;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test per-tenant masking guarantees in CI/CD?
- How would GDPR deletion requests propagate through streaming pipelines and downstream consumers?
